# Copy to .env.local for local development, or set in Vercel's project settings.
#
# Leave VITE_API_URL unset to run standalone. The app then stores accounts and
# portfolios in this browser -- but the CKKS encryption is real either way, so
# the privacy demonstration is genuine, not simulated.
#
# Set it to point at a running PENUMBRA backend:
#   VITE_API_URL=http://localhost:8000/api/v1
#
# Note the interop caveat in docs/SPEC_DEVIATIONS.md #11: this frontend uses
# node-seal (SEAL-native serialisation) and the Python backend uses TenSEAL
# (protobuf-wrapped). They are not yet wire-compatible, so a connected backend
# can serve auth and metadata but cannot yet exchange ciphertexts with this
# client. The app reports which mode it is in rather than failing quietly.

# VITE_API_URL=
